WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.998
Energy is what makes things happen.
It is in everything around you.

2
00:00:09.218 --> 00:00:12.143
You cannot hold it. You
can only see what it does.

3
00:00:12.643 --> 00:00:17.009
Let us go on an energy hunt. Six
things, and all six have energy.

4
00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:21.455
A moving ball has energy. The
faster it goes, the more it has.

5
00:00:21.675 --> 00:00:27.201
A stretched band has energy stored
in it, waiting. Let go, and it moves.

6
00:00:27.421 --> 00:00:32.947
Sound is energy travelling through the air.
Light and heat are energy from the Sun.

7
00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:37.997
Your food has energy stored in it
too. Energy is in every material.

8
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:43.418
Energy is not only electricity. A
hot cup and a loud drum have it too.

9
00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:47.030
Every movement and every
action needs energy.

10
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.197
Your muscles take it out of your
food, so that you can run and kick.

11
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:55.643
A lamp takes it from electricity.
A plant takes it from light.

12
00:00:55.863 --> 00:00:59.486
Take the energy away, and
nothing happens at all.

13
00:00:59.986 --> 00:01:03.608
Here is the big rule. Energy
cannot be made out of nothing.

14
00:01:03.828 --> 00:01:08.518
And it cannot be destroyed. It is
never used up, whatever people say.

15
00:01:08.738 --> 00:01:12.732
It can only be transferred:
moved from one thing to another.

16
00:01:12.952 --> 00:01:16.714
Or moved from one form to
another. Food to muscle.

17
00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:21.903
Then muscle to ball. Your kick sends
the energy into the ball, and it flies.

18
00:01:22.403 --> 00:01:27.325
Now drop a ball. Before you let go,
predict what the bounces will do.

19
00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:33.490
Held up high, the ball has stored energy.
As it falls, that becomes movement energy.

20
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.425
Bounce one. Thud! It comes
back up to three marks.

21
00:01:37.645 --> 00:01:43.404
Bounce two, and only two marks. Some
energy left as sound and warmth.

22
00:01:43.624 --> 00:01:47.617
Bounce three, just one mark. Each
bounce is lower than the last.

23
00:01:47.837 --> 00:01:51.878
None of it vanished. The bars
always add up to the same total.

24
00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:57.068
The ball hits the wall. Thump.
Some of its energy became sound.

25
00:01:57.288 --> 00:02:00.864
And some warmed the wall a
tiny bit. None of it was lost.

26
00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:06.703
A lamp is the same. Electricity goes in,
light comes out, and the bulb gets warm.

27
00:02:06.923 --> 00:02:12.032
A warm bulb is not broken. Every transfer
leaks a little to the surroundings.

28
00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:16.618
You read each bounce off the marked
scale. Then it goes in a table.

29
00:02:16.838 --> 00:02:21.436
First bounce, three marks. Second,
two marks. Third, one mark.

30
00:02:21.656 --> 00:02:26.160
Then you turn the table into a bar
chart, one bar for each bounce.

31
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:32.650
A falling staircase. That is the pattern:
energy transferred away every bounce.

32
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.004
Energy is in everything, and
in sound, light and heat.

33
00:02:37.224 --> 00:02:41.311
Nothing happens without it, and
it can never be made or destroyed.

34
00:02:41.531 --> 00:02:46.082
It is only transferred, and some
always leaks out to the surroundings.
